{"tool_name":"metidfyr","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"metidfyr","home":"https://github.com/agnesbrnb/MetIDfyR","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Open-Source R Package to Decipher Small-Molecule Drugs Metabolism Through High Resolution Mass Spectrometry.\n\nMetIDfyR is an open-source, cross-platform and versatile R script to predict and detect metabolites in mass spectrometry data (mzML) based on the raw formula of the drug of interest.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:08:27Z","last_update_date":"2025-02-27T15:46:01.807140Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Script"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:metidfyr","documentation":[{"type":["Citation instructions","Installation instructions","Quick start guide"],"url":"https://github.com/agnesbrnb/MetIDfyR"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Chemical formula","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0846"}},{"data":{"term":"Mass spectrometry data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2536"},"format":[{"term":"mzML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3244"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Natural product identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3803"},{"term":"Phasing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3454"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Plot","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2884"},"format":[{"term":"SVG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3604"}]},{"data":{"term":"Report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2048"},"format":[{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"}]}]}],"name":"MetIDfyR","owner":"agnesbarnabe","publication":[{"doi":"10.1021/acs.analchem.0c02281","metadata":{"abstract":"With recent advances in analytical chemistry, liquid chromatography high-resolution tandem mass spectrometry (LC-HRMS/MS) has become an essential tool for metabolite discovery and detection. Even if most of the common drug transformations have already been extensively described, manual search of drug metabolites in LC-HRMS/MS datasets is still a common practice in toxicology laboratories, complicating metabolite discovery. Furthermore, the availability of free open-source software for metabolite discovery is still limited. In this article, we present MetIDfyR, an open-source and cross-platform R package for in silico drug phase I/II biotransformation prediction and mass-spectrometric data mining. MetIDfyR has proven its efficacy for advanced metabolite identification in semi-complex and complex mixtures in in vitro or in vivo drug studies and is freely available at github.com/agnesblch/MetIDfyR.","authors":[{"name":"Andre F."},{"name":"Bailly-Chouriberry L."},{"name":"Barnabe A."},{"name":"Chabot B."},{"name":"Delcourt V."},{"name":"Garcia P."},{"name":"Loup B."},{"name":"Moulard Y."},{"name":"Popot M.-A."},{"name":"Trevisiol S."}],"citationCount":10,"date":"2020-10-06T00:00:00Z","journal":"Analytical Chemistry","title":"MetIDfyR: An Open-Source R Package to Decipher Small-Molecule Drug Metabolism through High-Resolution Mass Spectrometry"}}],"topic":[{"term":"Analytical chemistry","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3370"},{"term":"Drug metabolism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3375"},{"term":"Metabolomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3172"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"MetIDfyR","home":"https://bio.tools/metidfyr","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Open-Source R Package to Decipher Small-Molecule Drugs Metabolism Through High Resolution Mass Spectrometry.\n\nMetIDfyR is an open-source, cross-platform and versatile R script to predict and detect metabolites in mass spectrometry data (mzML) based on the raw formula of the drug of interest.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:metidfyr/script/github.com","@license":"https://cre